::
$HelpScreen
  ~@back;General.back
  @controls:Controls
  ~@editor;PlayScreen.editor
  @movement
  To move left press [A] or [LEFT ARROW], to move right
  press [D] or [RIGHT ARROW] and to jump press [W],
  [UP ARROW] or [SPACE].
  To flip the gravity press [G], [S] or [DOWN ARROW]
  and to reset press [R].
  $$Editor
    @layers
    The layers allow to place multiple blocks on the same position, blocks
    on lower layers appear behind blocks on higher layers.
    @block
    To select a block in the editor, click on the blue arrow next to the white
    X to select the type of the block and with the mouse wheel change the
    actual block.
    @move_door
    You can change the position of the doors by dragging them around the
    level and flip them by clicking on top.
    @move_player
    Similarly to move the player, use the controls or drag the player around.
    Remember that when a level is played, the gravity of the players is always
    pointing down for the player on the left and up for the one on the right.
